Modifications relative to the upstream work (Apache License 2.0 §4(b) notice):
- All `xai-*`/`xai-grok-*` crates renamed into the `alnair-*` namespace; the
  binary is `alnair`, the config directory is `~/.alnair`, and environment
  variables use the `ALNAIR_*` prefix.
- xAI/Grok service integrations removed or replaced: telemetry (Mixpanel,
  OpenTelemetry export, Sentry, trace upload), voice input, announcements,
  plugin marketplace, remote relay/gateway services, and the xAI OAuth and
  subscription-proxy endpoints.
- Re-targeted as a provider-agnostic agent. First-party endpoints default to
  the Kimi Code subscription API (api.kimi.com/coding/v1) and the Moonshot
  open platform (api.moonshot.cn/v1, api.moonshot.ai/v1); on top of those,
  subscription OAuth is wired for Kimi Code, Claude Pro/Max, ChatGPT (Codex),
  GitHub Copilot and xAI Grok, API keys for the open platforms, and
  user-declared providers by base URL. Self-update uses GitHub Releases
  (github.com).

Modifications relative to Kigi (Apache License 2.0 §4(b) notice):
- Crate, binary, config-directory and environment-variable names changed from
  the `kigi-*`/`kigi`/`~/.kigi`/`KIGI_*` forms to the `alnair-*`/`alnair`/
  `~/.alnair`/`ALNAIR_*` forms throughout.
- Identity and release surfaces rewritten: the README, the "one identity"
  section, the install scripts and the self-update release source now point at
  the Alnair project (GitHub Releases) rather than Kigi's Gitea forge.
- Login and logout were replaced by `alnair connect` / `/connect`, a single
  provider picker that is also the only disconnect surface; the primary-scope
  `logout` command was removed.
- NEW: a browser client, `alnair web` (`crates/codegen/alnair-web` plus the
  `web/` SvelteKit harness). It is a client of the shared leader rather than a
  second agent, and adds an embedded single-binary SPA, a cookie + `Origin`
  authenticated WebSocket bridge, a native directory picker endpoint, and
  per-session client fan-out.
- NEW: multi-terminal session UX in the pager — leader-by-default resolution,
  startup auto-attach to a matching session, a global session tab strip (F2)
  that spans repositories and persists to `~/.alnair/run/pager_tabs.json`, a
  dashboard with session CRUD, and an app-level directory picker with three
  distinct purposes.
- NEW: an interactive terminal pane (F3) that owns its own PTY, forwards input,
  paste and resize, replays a ring buffer on reopen, and is fed by the extracted
  `alnair-terminal-screen` emulator crate.
- NEW: config hot-reload. A debounced watcher feeds a reloader that diffs and
  dispatches to two transports (ACP stream injection under a leader, direct
  dispatch in the in-process TUI), covering `[platforms.*]`, `[model.*]`,
  `[mcp_servers]`, `[skills]`, `[compat]`, `[ui]`, and `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md`
  / rules `*.md`.
- NEW: a workspace lesson library (`[lessons]`, `/lessons`, `~/.alnair/lessons/`):
  harness postmortems captured from the goal strategist and graph node
  archives, distilled deterministically, and injected once at the start of the
  next session in the same workspace.
- The local release line was reset to 0.1.1 when the project stopped presenting
  itself as a Kimi Code community build; it stands at 0.1.2 here.

